      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a profound and exhausting realization when you feel like the struggle itself is the only constant. When everything feels fixed and insurmountable, the urge to simply stop fighting is incredibly powerful. It's okay to acknowledge that exhaustion, and sometimes the most courageous thing is to stop trying to force a path forward. If you feel like you've hit a dead end, talking to someone who understands this deep weariness can offer a different perspective on what \"next\" might look like.",
